{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "An issuer that left Agreely, as the /verify page reads it. The record is /c/{slug}/departure.json beside the did.json of a did:web:<host>:c:<slug> issuer (departureUrl; any other DID has none). It is asked for only once the receipt's signature held and the issuer DID document the resolver returned says deactivated (the boolean true), and that document names the issuer (else: unreadable, nothing asked). A record counts only when it names this exact issuer DID, says status purged, and carries two real civil days sealedOn <= purgedOn: else unreadable. An HTTP error (a 404 included), a network error or a body that is not JSON is unreachable, never a reading that the issuer stayed. phase: the signing instant (recordedAt from receipt version 2, grantedAt otherwise) read on its UTC day: after when that day is strictly after purgedOn + 1 day, before when it precedes sealedOn, during otherwise, unknown when the instant does not parse. issuerDeparture: pass (before, during), fail (after: overall failed, and the registry is not asked: companyKeyRegistry skipped), unavailable (unreachable, unreadable, unknown: nothing changes). counts: a departure speaks for the issuer (and a consent read in force stops reading withdrawal active) when it is after, or when companyKeyOf confirmed the key (companyKeyVerdict authentic, null when not read). A live issuer, a deactivated member that is not the boolean true, and checkDeparture false: the fields are absent and nothing is asked. record: receipts/a3v4.bundle.json (recordedAt 2026-06-02T09:00:00Z) with resolver receipts/v4-did-documents.json, its issuer document patched with issuerDocument, no rpcUrl, the departure URL answered with `answer` (status and a JSON body, or text; null: a network error). cases: `file` verified with resolver `documents`, the receipt issuer's document patched with issuerDocument (null: as is), `http` answering GET by exact URL (absent: a network error; a PHP httpGet answers the body of a 2xx and null otherwise), `answers` the chain as in recorded-v4.json (null: no rpcUrl; else rpcUrl https://rpc.test, chainId 84532), `options` passed as is. asked: every GET URL, in order. expect is read field by field as in recorded-v4.json.",
